 "notes": "Stack controller: damped-least-squares IK (position + orientation, nullspace bias toward a multi-seed global IK solution) drives the grasp site with a rate-limited Cartesian target. Hand orientation: palm down with 0.2 rad fingers-down tilt; yaw chosen among the 4 cube-diagonal candidates by IK reachability/joint-margin scoring (grasp across the cube's diagonal so the two fingers and thumb self-center the cube). Phases: pre-curl fingers (closure 0.38) -> move above target -> descend (stall/contact detection) -> close to 1.0 -> lift to z=0.92, measure cube offset in hand -> move above destination (re-choose yaw if needed) -> slow descent to dest+5.6cm -> release -> slow retreat; verifies the stack and retries grasp/place if it failed or the cube was lost. Joint-space servo-sag compensation (low-passed target-measured error) for weak motors. Tested ~95/97 on nominal practice seeds and on weak_motors / heavy_slippery / noisy_sensing variants. Known weaknesses: no obstacle awareness, so a neighbouring cube close to the target (within ~8 cm on the thumb side) can be knocked by the open thumb/fingers (one drop observed); retries after a bad placement can push cubes near the table edge off.",
